    "body": "`btck_transaction_create` and `btck_block_create` ignore any bytes after the serialized object, so the object's serialized length does not match the buffer.\n\nI return null when bytes remain, as for other malformed input, and say so in the header. Two new checks in `test_kernel` append one byte to a valid transaction and to a valid block. They fail on master and pass with the change. The other kernel tests and the unit tests pass.\n\nThis is one of several PRs from a large audit of Bitcoin Core that I did with the help of LLM tools. The audit produced its evidence all at once, which is why the PRs arrive together. I understand each change fully and will answer review questions myself.\n",
