        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree d26f682977056443c769b40d732d1fc1f558d2f3\nparent a773e1e33b349dc819b5a0edc1c7a4839dc73b48\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792824888 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1792827553 +0200\n\nkernel: reject trailing bytes in object creation\n\nbtck_transaction_create and btck_block_create deserialize one object and\nignore any bytes that follow it. The object's serialized length then\ndiffers from the buffer's.\n\nI return null when bytes remain after the object, as for other malformed\ninput, and say so in the header. The kernel tests pass a valid\ntransaction and a valid block with one extra byte.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRJ5SMZs3eEinN+Lb4iedqLwmlHIAUCatxgoRsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQInnai8JpRyCe9AD9FSsEbbE2VtZ9jr/Eb9EZ\n9FDY2YPkXqUZ2g3yfpeoOIYBAPUX6Gxtm5GxdQBhYmSwLfcmLOvxJNcw+t+2sydB\nrmYG\n=SVvu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
